From u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com  Wed Jul 29 13:08:58 2015
From: u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com (Karl Broman)
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2015 13:08:58 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rqtl-disc] Get the p-value for all SNPs in QTL calculation
Message-ID: <pzG0K5uPZq0.FRGhQrv9BQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <pzG0K5uPZq0.e2dIJYX4BQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <pzG0K5uPZq0.e2dIJYX4BQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/pzG0K5uPZq0/m/FRGhQrv9BQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The p-value is the proportion of permutations with LOD score greater than or equal to the observed LOD, so you could go through the LODs for each SNP and calculate those proportions.

# example analysis and permutations
data(fake.bc)
fake.bc <- calc.genoprob(fake.bc, step=2.5)
out <- scanone(fake.bc, method="hk")
operm <- scanone(fake.bc, method="hk", n.perm=1000)

# calculate p-values
pval <- sapply(out[,3], function(a,b) mean(b >= a), operm)

# the same thing, via a for loop
pval <- rep(NA, nrow(out))
for(i in 1:nrow(out))
    pval[i] <- mean(operm >= out[i,3])

karl

