Hey Karl -- each row in your matrix provides an estimate of the distribution of cutoffs under a set of (n_pheno) tests.
The distribution of, e.g., maximum cutoffs, for a set of the above distributional estimates would be estimated as you indicate... with a more rows (n_perm) providing a better estimate of this "maximum cutoff distribution".

